      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Worldwide Express (part of ShipStation Global) had built something big: approximately $5 billion in systemwide revenue, over 75 less-than-truckload (LTL) carriers and more than 130,000 customers.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:31.162Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Worldwide Express worked with AWS and LTM to build a multi-agentic AI solution with Amazon Bedrock that plugs directly into their transportation management system (TMS), SpeedShip.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:31.162Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Six months after launch, the company reported a 75 percent reduction in active exceptions, a 4-week improvement in time-to-cash, $1M annual savings, and a one-time $10M free cash flow infusion.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:31.162Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In June 2025, Worldwide Express engaged the AWS Business Transformation & Value Advisory team to identify 19 automation opportunities across the Order-to-Cash lifecycle.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:31.162Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Knowing the business value of exceptions automation, Worldwide Express moved from assessment to production in less than 6 months.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:31.162Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Amazon Bedrock provides AI reasoning, and Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) is the engine.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:31.162Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Building the framework directly on Amazon EC2, with Amazon Bedrock providing inference, keeps that orchestration logic fully in the team’s hands and supports open source agent libraries.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:31.162Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Each agent runs on Amazon EC2 with Auto Scaling, uses an agent framework with its own prompt, tools, and carrier knowledge base, and calls Amazon Bedrock for model inference.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:31.162Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: Worldwide Express’s AI-powered exception handling architecture on AWS",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-worldwide-express-automated-freight-exceptions-with-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T17:32:20.000Z",
